Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:09:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 124/638] [AROS] Use full-width V8 before sparse MMU
 reservations

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-phase-3
AI_STATUS: complete
ROOT_CAUSE: Hosted run 0124 reached V8 process initialization but the main sandbox requires at least 8 GiB of sparse virtual address space; hosted AROS is already at its 4090 MB maximum and the pre-MMU allocator physically backs reservations. A 4 GiB pointer-compression cage would fail next even with the sandbox disabled.
FIX_REASON: Advance V8 to its supported full-width, uncaged AROS configuration so all cage-derived features are disabled coherently until OPAL/MMU supplies sparse reservations.
SCOPE: v8 submodule pointer
VALIDATION: Headless GN regenerated 13,556 targets and both target and host V8 graphs contain zero compression, sandbox, external-code-space, or cppgc cage-derived defines; artifact 27 captures the exact sandbox OOM.
RISK: V8 uses wider heap pointers and no process sandbox during bring-up; this is an explicit temporary security/performance tradeoff, not the final MMU-backed configuration.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: run 0124 sandbox OOM -> V8 d1700ca898 -> hosted run 0125
---
 v8 | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

